## Findings (grounded)

### C2 — root cause CONFIRMED by direct probe (no question needed)

- `SystemSettingsPanel.tsx`, `app/schemas/system_config.py`, `app/routes/system_config.py` are all UNTRACKED (`??` in `git status`).
- `app/routes/routes.py` is M (modified) — adds `from app.routes import ... system_config` + `app.include_router(system_config.router, ...)` + DI override.
- The new TSX/TS/py files were saved **2026-06-30 08:45–10:07 EDT**.
- `npm run build` was run **2026-06-30 10:17** — fresh `dist/assets/DeviceConfig-De48FDTo.js` contains both `SystemSettings` render code AND `DfrBoards` body (grep-confirmed). Build is good.
- `automation-service` last started **Mon 2026-06-29 18:31:50 EDT** — BEFORE the new route file was saved.
- Direct probe with the correct `X-API-Key`: `GET /api/config` → **HTTP 404 `{"error":"Not found"}`**.
- Python imports route modules at startup (`register_routes` in `routes/routes.py`); the running process has NOT imported `system_config.router`.
- Therefore SystemSettingsPanel mounts, calls `apiClient.getConfig()` → 404 → `loadConfig` catch → `config=null` → renders `Failed to load settings` (line 440 of SystemSettingsPanel.tsx).

**Fix for C2 is trivial — one command, no plan slot needed:**
`sudo systemctl restart automation-service`

After restart: `system_config.router` loads, `/api/config` returns 200, panel renders.
I will present this as a found fact in the next message and let the user verify
before deciding whether C2 even belongs in the plan.

### C1 — relay matrix (need owner input)

Current per-box elements (from `RelayChannelBox.tsx`):
1. `RelayGlyph` — vertical colored bar, visual state
2. `RelayStatusLed` — colored dot (may duplicate glyph)
3. Header label `R{n} · CH {channel}`
4. `locationLabel` (or "Unassigned location")
5. Status badge button — text ON/IDLE/MM:SS, tone active/idle/unknown
6. `deviceLabel` (or "Unassigned")
7. `typeLabel` — readable device type
8. `elapsedLabel` — `formatElapsedSince(lastStateChangeAt)`

Panel-variant chrome (from `RelayChannelMatrix.tsx`):
- "16-CH Relay Module" header
- "MCP23017 · SainSmart layout" subtitle
- `TerminalStrip` decorations (bank A / bank B)
- "Left (R 1–8)" / "Right (R 16–9)" column headers
- Row-number gutter (1..8 both sides)
- "Low-level Input" footer strip

"Timing fields" candidates — what could be "not working":
- Timer menu actions (`timer-5m/10m/30m/1h`) → `manualTimersByChannel` state, countdown rendered via `statusByChannel` (`MM:SS` text).
- The `elapsedLabel` since last state change.
- The 5s `refreshRelayState` polling interval.
- Auto-completion effect when countdown hits zero (lines 295-349 of DeviceManager.tsx).

Need user to say which elements are junk and which "timing" is broken.

### C3 — DFR panel wasted space (structural, need owner input)

Current layout (`DfrBoardsPanel.tsx`):
- 3-column grid of board cards, each `aspect-square` (forces square)
- 2 channels per card, each with select dropdown + display-name input + Save button + "Device key: <name>" mono text
- Square aspect on a 2-channel card leaves 30-50% vertical whitespace

Potential junk / never-used fields:
- "Device key: <name>" mono text under each channel
- The per-channel "Display name" inline rename (only useful if lights get renamed often)
- The standalone `aspect-square` constraint
- The 3-column grid when there are exactly 3 boards

